This sentinel file is committed so that `//go:embed all:dist` in embed.go
always matches at least one file, even on a fresh clone before any
`npm run build` has been run. Without it, `go build` fails with
"pattern all:dist: cannot embed directory dist: contains no embeddable files".

It is never served to clients — router.go only serves index.html and assets/.
vite.config.ts sets emptyOutDir: false so this file survives every build.

NOTE: do NOT let stale hashed bundles accumulate in this dir across local
`make run` / `make build-admin` runs. They are harmless for local dev (the new
index.html only references the latest), but historically they caused a subtle
docker build bug: the Dockerfile's builder stage `COPY backend/ ./` would drag
the stale local dist into the image, and when the spa stage's fresh build
failed to land at the expected path (a WORKDIR bug, now fixed), go:embed
silently picked up the STALE local dist — serving an old admin SPA after
deploy. The Dockerfile now sets the spa stage WORKDIR correctly so the fresh
build always wins, but keeping this dir clean is still good hygiene.
